  ('finance/quantitative-foundations/rates-and-returns/core-concepts', 'finance', 'finance/quantitative-foundations/rates-and-returns', 'Core Concepts', 'core-concepts', 'What an interest rate is, and the three equivalent ways to read it: as a required rate of return, as a discount rate used to bring future cash flows to the present, and as the opportunity cost of current consumption. An interest rate as the sum of a real risk-free rate plus premiums that compensate investors for bearing distinct types of risk — inflation, default, liquidity, and maturity risk. And how a return is measured over time, including how to calculate it.', 0, 2),
